╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ efficient_circular_ry_cz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The original ansatz used 24 parameters per block (RY, RZ, CZ-chain, RZ) which, when       │
│                          │ repeated across 3 uploads and 2 repeats (6 blocks total), resulted in 146 trainable       │
│                          │ parameters. While accurate, this is relatively parameter-heavy for an 8-qubit system.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This evolution optimizes the ansatz by:                                                   │
│                          │ 1.  **Reducing Parameters:** Moving to a 16-parameter-per-block structure (RY,            │
│                          │ CZ-circular, RY). This reduces the total parameter count from 146 to 98, significantly    │
│                          │ boosting the `parameter_efficiency` metric.                                               │
│                          │ 2.  **Circular Entanglement:** Replacing the linear CZ chain with a staggered circular CZ │
│                          │ arrangement. This ensures better connectivity and information flow across all qubits,     │
│                          │ especially important for the 28-feature IsingZZ map.                                      │
│                          │ 3.  **Basis Flexibility:** Using two layers of RY rotations separated by entanglers. This │
│                          │ allows the model to rotate the phase-encoded features into the Z-basis more effectively   │
│                          │ than the original RZ-heavy configuration, which is often redundant when followed by       │
│                          │ phase-coupling (IsingZZ) or phase-gates (CZ).                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This refinement targets a higher combined score by improving parameter efficiency and     │
│                          │ reducing the gate count/depth while maintaining the high classification accuracy.         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
