│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ selective_param_sharing_efficient                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current seed achieves excellent accuracy (98% test, 99% validation) but uses 146      │
│                          │ parameters with relatively low parameter efficiency (0.01). The key insight is that the   │
│                          │ ansatz achieves such high performance that many parameters may be redundant.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current approach: Independent RY and RZ rotations for all 8 qubits (24 parameters per     │
│                          │ block × 6 blocks = 144 circuit parameters).                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New approach: Selective parameter sharing to reduce degrees of freedom:                   │
│                          │ - Keep individual RY parameters for each qubit (crucial for feature-dependent rotations)  │
│                          │ → 8 unique params                                                                         │
│                          │ - Share RZ pre-entanglement parameters in pairs (qubits 0-1 share one, 2-3 share another, │
│                          │ etc.) → 2 unique params                                                                   │
│                          │ - Share RZ post-entanglement parameters similarly → 2 unique params                       │
│                          │ - Maintain the effective CZ entanglement chain                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters per block from 24 to 12 (50% reduction), giving 72 circuit        │
│                          │ parameters total. With readout params: 74 total (vs 146).                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Parameter efficiency improves from 0.98/146=0.0067 to 0.98/74=0.0132 (2× improvement),    │
│                          │ directly boosting the combined score. The shared structure maintains sufficient           │
│                          │ expressiveness while reducing overfitting risk (train-test gap can only improve or stay   │
│                          │ similar). Convergence should be faster with fewer parameters to tune.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Slightly increased learning rate compensates for the reduced parameter space              │
│                          │ dimensionality.                                                                           │
