╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_entanglement_efficiency                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses a relatively large parameter set (146 total) with separate RZ     │
│                          │ layers before and after a simple CZ line of entanglement. To improve parameter efficiency │
│                          │ while maintaining accuracy, I propose replacing the post-entanglement RZ layer with       │
│                          │ parametrized CRZ (controlled rotation Z) gates in a line pattern. This consolidates       │
│                          │ expressiveness: instead of having parameters in separate RZ gates and no parameters in CZ │
│                          │ gates, we integrate the rotation parameters directly into the entanglement layer via CRZ. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key benefits:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter reduction**: Reduces from 24 params/block (8 RY + 8 RZ pre + 8 RZ post) to │
│                          │ 23 params/block (8 RY + 8 RZ + 7 CRZ), saving ~1.4% of circuit parameters per block, or   │
│                          │ ~4% overall (146 → 140).                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. **Better parameter utilization**: CRZ gates parametrically couple qubits, allowing     │
│                          │ rotation angles to directly influence entanglement strength, which can improve            │
│                          │ trainability and generalization.                                                          │
│                          │ 3. **Maintained expressiveness**: Two layers of single-qubit rotations plus parametrized  │
│                          │ two-qubit entanglement preserve the model's capability to learn complex decision          │
│                          │ boundaries.                                                                               │
│                          │ 4. **Faster convergence potential**: Fewer redundant parameters can lead to faster        │
│                          │ convergence (evidenced by improved parameter efficiency helping optimization dynamics).   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The structure becomes:                                                                    │
│                          │ - RY rotations (8 params, independent)                                                    │
│                          │ - RZ rotations (8 params, independent)                                                    │
│                          │ - CRZ line: each of the 7 qubit-pairs (0-1, 1-2, ..., 6-7) has a parametrized             │
│                          │ controlled-Z rotation (7 params, independent)                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This removes the post-entanglement RZ layer, which was somewhat redundant given the       │
│                          │ flexible pre-entanglement RZ and the now-parametrized entanglement layer.                 │
