│ patch_name               │ cnot_ry_rz_brickwork                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The previous candidate (Program 3) achieved 100% accuracy with a 1.46 score using a       │
│                          │ double-RY and double-CZ brick-wall structure (16 unique parameters per block). This       │
│                          │ proposed architecture aims to further minimize the validation loss and improve            │
│                          │ convergence speed by:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1.  **Diversifying Rotation Axes**: Replacing the second RY layer with an RZ layer.       │
│                          │ Alternating RY and RZ rotations is a common strategy in hardware-efficient ansatze to     │
│                          │ ensure the circuit can explore the entire Bloch sphere more effectively.                  │
│                          │ 2.  **Stronger Entanglement**: Replacing the CZ gates with CNOT gates. CNOTs provide a    │
│                          │ more direct basis transformation (X-flip) compared to the phase-only interaction of CZ,   │
│                          │ which can lead to faster training on binary feature tasks.                                │
│                          │ 3.  **Circular Connectivity**: Maintaining the brick-wall pattern (even and odd pairs)    │
│                          │ including the (7,0) wrap-around to ensure high connectivity across all 8 qubits, which is │
│                          │ critical for the global mean-Z readout.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This maintains the 16-parameter count (98 total parameters including gain/bias) while     │
│                          │ improving expressivity.                                                                   │
