│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ orthogonal_controlled_rotations                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This approach implements a hardware-efficient ansatz (HEA) with an alternating            │
│                          │ "brickwork" pattern of parametrized controlled rotations. Specifically, it uses           │
│                          │ independent RY rotations on all qubits followed by two layers of CRX gates (even and odd  │
│                          │ pairs).                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The use of RY as the base rotation layer allows for optimal population transfer between   │
│                          │ $|0\rangle$ and $|1\rangle$, while the CRX gates provide entanglement via an orthogonal   │
│                          │ rotation axis (X), creating a more expressive Hilbert space representation for binary     │
│                          │ classification. The brickwork connectivity (even pairs, then odd pairs) ensures global    │
│                          │ entanglement across the 8-qubit register within each block.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ By using 16 parameters per block (8 RY + 8 CRX), we maintain the same parameter count as  │
│                          │ the highest-performing seed (Seed 2) while potentially improving the loss landscape and   │
│                          │ generalization by mixing Y and X-axis operations. This architecture is designed to reach  │
│                          │ high accuracy quickly while keeping the circuit depth manageable.                         │
