│ patch_description        │ This candidate replaces the sparse shared-RZ/CZ seed with a symmetric, parameter-tied     │
│                          │ brickwork block. It keeps the same fixed training loop and measurements, but uses a more  │
│                          │ expressive and better-conditioned ansatz per upload: independent entry RY rotations,      │
│                          │ local CZ entangling, shared cross-half RZ layers, cross-half CRY couplings, shifted CZ    │
│                          │ entangling, and a mirrored exit RY layer that reuses the entry parameters. This structure │
│                          │ preserves parameter efficiency while increasing mixing across the 8 qubits, which should  │
│                          │ help reduce validation/test loss and accelerate convergence without changing the          │
│                          │ program’s inputs or outputs.                                                              │
