│ patch_name               │ tied_ring_mirror                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite keeps the fixed training loop and feature map unchanged, but replaces the    │
│                          │ ansatz with a much more parameter-efficient symmetric block.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new block uses:                                                                       │
│                          │ - a full 8-qubit RY initialization,                                                       │
│                          │ - staggered CZ entanglement across the ring,                                              │
│                          │ - pair-shared RZ phases on opposite qubits,                                               │
│                          │ - then a mirrored second half that reuses the same parameters again.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This ties the two within-block repeats together, reducing the block to 12 unique          │
│                          │ parameters instead of the previous 24, which lowers the total parameter count to 74 and   │
│                          │ should improve generalization and optimization stability while preserving enough          │
│                          │ expressivity for the binary classification task.                                          │
