│ patch_name               │ shared_8_param_ring_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ I’m tightening the ansatz into a parameter-shared, low-redundancy block that still keeps  │
│                          │ the circuit expressive.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main change is to reuse the same 8 trainable keys across multiple single-qubit        │
│                          │ layers, instead of allocating separate keys for every layer. This directly reduces the    │
│                          │ unique circuit parameters per block while preserving a strong inductive bias: a local RY  │
│                          │ warm-start, a ring CZ entangler, a shared RZ refinement, a long-range CRY bridge, a       │
│                          │ shifted CZ ring, and a final shared RX layer.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should help:                                                                     │
│                          │ - fewer unique parameters improves parameter efficiency and usually reduces overfitting   │
│                          │ - shared weights across sublayers encourage smoother optimization and better              │
│                          │ generalization                                                                            │
│                          │ - mixed-axis rotations plus two entangling topologies keep enough expressivity for the    │
│                          │ binary classification task                                                                │
│                          │ - reduced circuit size should also help convergence speed under the fixed Adam training   │
│                          │ loop                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This follows the recommendation to tie parameters across repeated substructures, but in a │
│                          │ stronger form: the same 8 keys are reused throughout the block.                           │
