                         Patch Metadata - Gen 16/20 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ simplify_to_crx_with_control_swaps                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current program's ANSATZ_SPEC is overly complex (29 gates) with mixed fixed CNOT      │
│                          │ gates, parametrized CRY gates, and RZ intermediate rotations, resulting in:               │
│                          │ - Higher parameter count (122 vs. 98 in the best prior program)                           │
│                          │ - Worse accuracy (0.99 vs. 1.00)                                                          │
│                          │ - Slower convergence (240 vs. 150 steps)                                                  │
│                          │ - Larger validation/test loss (0.08 vs. 0.03)                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second prior program achieved the best combined score (1.50) using a minimalist       │
│                          │ CRX-only design with 16 gates and 98 parameters. This design:                             │
│                          │ 1. Uses a simple RY basis layer                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Applies CRX parametrized gates in two layers (even and odd qubit pairs)                │
│                          │ 3. Requires fewer parameters and gates, reducing circuit complexity                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose to:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Revert to the efficient CRX-based structure (8 RY + 8 CRX)                             │
│                          │ 2. Apply the recommended control-target swaps to half the second-layer CRX gates:         │
│                          │    - Swap (3,4) → (4,3) and (7,0) → (0,7)                                                 │
│                          │    - Keep (1,2) and (5,6) unchanged                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best-performing minimal architecture with diversified entanglement      │
│                          │ symmetry via inverse conditional rotations, without adding extra gates or parameters.     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
