│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_shared_rz_readout_layer                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz achieves excellent accuracy (1.00) but shows suboptimal convergence    │
│                          │ speed (210 steps vs. 150 in the best prior program) and slightly higher validation loss   │
│                          │ (0.04 vs. 0.03). The depth and gate count are also higher than necessary.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the expert recommendation, I propose adding a final shared-parameter RZ phase   │
│                          │ layer after all ansatz blocks. This adds only 1 new parameter but 8 gates to fine-tune    │
│                          │ the measurement basis globally. This approach:                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Addresses the measurement calibration bottleneck with minimal parameter overhead       │
│                          │ 2. Leverages the success of simple single-qubit rotations observed in prior programs      │
│                          │ 3. Maintains the current block structure while enhancing the final readout rotation       │
│                          │ 4. Should improve convergence speed by allowing the network to globally adjust the        │
│                          │ measurement axis                                                                          │
│                          │ 5. Adds negligible computational complexity (8 RZ gates) with only 1 shared parameter     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The shared parameter `"rz_end"` is reused across all 8 qubits, making it an efficient     │
│                          │ fine-tuning knob for the measurement basis. This is similar to how gain/bias calibration  │
│                          │ works in the readout, but embedded within the quantum circuit.                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
